<title>USA: NY business loans rose $36 mln in Dec 4 week.</title>
<headline>NY business loans rose $36 mln in Dec 4 week.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Commercial and industrial loans at the six major New York banks, excluding acceptances, rose $36 million to $43,239 million in the week ended December 4, the Federal Reserve Bank of New York said.</p>
<p>Including acceptances, loans rose $5 million to $43,495 million.</p>
<p>Commercial paper outstanding nationally rose $4,148 million to $769,446 million.</p>
<p>-- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660</p>
</text>
